    public TreeAnalysisResult analyzeTreePaths(TreeNode root, Integer targetSum) {
        TreeAnalysisResult result = new TreeAnalysisResult();
        if (root == null) {
            return result;
        }

        List<Integer> currentPath = new ArrayList<>();
        traverseTree(root, currentPath, 0, result, targetSum);

        return result;
    }

    private void traverseTree(TreeNode node, List<Integer> currentPath, int currentSum,
                             TreeAnalysisResult result, Integer targetSum) {
        if (node == null) {
            return;
        }

        currentPath.add(node.val);
        currentSum += node.val;

        if (node.left == null && node.right == null) {
            result.paths.add(new ArrayList<>(currentPath));
            result.leafCount++;

            int currentDepth = currentPath.size() - 1;
            if (currentDepth > result.maxDepth) {
                result.maxDepth = currentDepth;
            }

            if (targetSum != null && currentSum == targetSum) {
                result.hasPathSum = true;
            }
        }

        traverseTree(node.left, currentPath, currentSum, result, targetSum);
        traverseTree(node.right, currentPath, currentSum, result, targetSum);

        currentPath.remove(currentPath.size() - 1);
    }
}
```

### Explanation
- **TreeNode**: Represents a node in the binary tree with a value and left/right children.
- **TreeAnalysisResult**: Stores analysis results including paths, max depth, leaf count, and path sum check.
- **TreePathAnalyzer**: Implements the analysis logic:
